<!-- What Is Fire-Rated Drylining -->
<h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">What Is Fire-Rated Drylining?</h2>
<p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Fire-rated drylining is a specialist construction system that provides timed fire protection for walls and ceilings. The fire rating — measured in minutes — indicates how long the partition can resist fire without allowing flames or extreme heat to pass through. In a fire, every minute counts, and fire-rated drylining gives people crucial time to evacuate and firefighters time to respond.</p>
<p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">At <strong>Drylining Edinburgh</strong>, we supply and install fire-rated drylining systems using certified materials from British Gypsum and Knauf. Our installations are designed to meet or exceed the fire resistance requirements specified in Scottish Building Standards Section 2 (Fire), and we provide full documentation with every project. This is essential for Edinburgh's dense urban environment, where multi-storey tenements, student accommodation, and regeneration projects like the NCC Engine Shed and Sighthill developments all require certified fire protection systems.</p>

<!-- What We Offer -->
<h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Our Fire-Rated Drylining Services</h2>
<ul style="list-style:disc;padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;font-size:1.0625rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
  <li>30-minute fire-rated drylining for residential properties</li>
  <li>60-minute fire-rated partitions for commercial buildings</li>
  <li>90 and 120-minute fire-rated systems for high-risk areas</li>
  <li>Fire-rated wall and ceiling installations</li>
  <li>Cavity barrier installation at floor and ceiling levels</li>
  <li>Intumescent sealant application around edges and penetrations</li>
  <li>Fire-rated door frame integration</li>
  <li>Upgrading existing drylining to fire-rated specifications</li>
</ul>

<!-- Where Fire-Rated Drylining Is Required -->
<h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Where Fire-Rated Drylining Is Required</h2>
<p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Scottish Building Standards Section 2 specifies fire resistance requirements for most building types. In Edinburgh and the Lothians, we regularly install fire-rated drylining in:</p>
<ul style="list-style:disc;padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;font-size:1.0625rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
  <li>Multi-storey apartment blocks across Edinburgh (EH1–EH36 postcodes)</li>
  <li>Student accommodation — Edinburgh is a major student city with thousands of halls and HMOs</li>
  <li>Hotels along Princes Street, George Street, and the New Town area</li>
  <li>Office buildings in the Financial District, St James, and Leith Walk</li>
  <li>Schools and education facilities across the City of Edinburgh council area</li>
  <li>Healthcare and care home refurbishments</li>
  <li>Retail and leisure complexes including St James Quarter, Orchard Brae, and Staling Mall</li>
  <li>Multi-unit housing developments and townhouse conversions</li>
</ul>

<!-- Materials & Specifications -->
<h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Materials &amp; Specifications</h2>
<p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">We use premium fire-rated materials from trusted manufacturers to ensure your drylining delivers the fire performance and durability you need.</p>
<ul style="list-style:disc;padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;font-size:1.0625rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
  <li>British Gypsum Gyproc Fireline fire-rated plasterboard</li>
  <li>Knauf Diamant fire-rated plasterboard for high-performance applications</li>
  <li>Cavity barriers (steel, mineral wool, and intumescent types)</li>
  <li>Intumescent sealants for joints, edges, and service penetrations</li>
  <li>Metal C-studs and U-tracks (50mm, 70mm, 92mm profiles)</li>
