<!-- FAQ -->
<h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Frequently Asked Questions about Fire-Rated Drylining</h2>
<div>
  <div style="padding:20px;margin-bottom:12px;background:var(--white);border-radius:var(--radius);border:1px solid var(--border);">
    <h3 style="font-size:16px;margin-bottom:8px;color:var(--primary);">What is fire-rated drylining?</h3>
    <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-light);margin:0;">Fire-rated drylining uses specialist plasterboard and construction methods to provide fire protection for walls and ceilings. The fire rating indicates how long the partition can resist fire — from 30 minutes up to 120 minutes — giving people time to evacuate and firefighters time to respond.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="padding:20px;margin-bottom:12px;background:var(--white);border-radius:var(--radius);border:1px solid var(--border);">
    <h3 style="font-size:16px;margin-bottom:8px;color:var(--primary);">Which buildings require fire-rated drylining?</h3>
    <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-light);margin:0;">Fire-rated drylining is required in multi-storey buildings, flats, student accommodation, hotels, hospitals, schools, and commercial buildings with more than one storey. Part B of the Scottish Building Standards specifies fire resistance requirements for most building types.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="padding:20px;margin-bottom:12px;background:var(--white);border-radius:var(--radius);border:1px solid var(--border);">
    <h3 style="font-size:16px;margin-bottom:8px;color:var(--primary);">What fire ratings do you provide?</h3>
    <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-light);margin:0;">We provide fire-rated drylining from 30 minutes up to 120 minutes, using combinations of fire-rated plasterboard, cavity barriers, intumescent sealants, and specialist framing systems to meet the required fire performance.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="padding:20px;margin-bottom:12px;background:var(--white);border-radius:var(--radius);border:1px solid var(--border);">
    <h3 style="font-size:16px;margin-bottom:8px;color:var(--primary);">Do fire-rated walls look different from standard walls?</h3>
    <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-light);margin:0;">No. Fire-rated drylining looks exactly like standard drylining — smooth, professional, and ready for decoration. The fire protection is built into the construction, not visible from the finished surface.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="padding:20px;margin-bottom:12px;background:var(--white);border-radius:var(--radius);border:1px solid var(--border);">
    <h3 style="font-size:16px;margin-bottom:8px;color:var(--primary);">Can fire-rated drylining be used in existing buildings?</h3>
    <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-light);margin:0;">Yes. We can upgrade existing drylining to fire-rated specifications or install new fire-rated partitions during refurbishment projects. Our team can assess your building and recommend the appropriate fire rating.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="padding:20px;margin-bottom:12px;background:var(--white);border-radius:var(--radius);border:1px solid var(--border);">
    <h3 style="font-size:16px;margin-bottom:8px;color:var(--primary);">What certifications do your fire-rated installations carry?</h3>
    <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-light);margin:0;">All our fire-rated drylining work uses British Gypsum and Knauf products that carry manufacturer certifications. We provide documentation with each installation confirming compliance with Scottish Building Standards Section 2 (Fire).</p>
  </div>
  <div style="padding:20px;margin-bottom:12px;background:var(--white);border-radius:var(--radius);border:1px solid var(--border);">
